# Custom Page Interactive Sections

`form`, `qa`, `survey`, `poll`, and `vote` are ordinary sections in the
authoritative `pages.content` array. Their definitions and records remain in
their config object; no second response store exists.

Authenticated participation uses
`POST /pages/{id}/sections/{sectionId}/responses`. Moderation uses the matching
PATCH/DELETE record routes and the page security policy. The repository locks
the page row, validates the stored definition, applies limits/idempotency, and
rewrites the document atomically.

Ordinary builder saves also lock the page and preserve the current interactive
records, preventing a stale editor snapshot from erasing responses. Duplicate
pages clear records and result summaries.

Viewer payloads are caller-specific: managers see management data, participants
see only their permitted state, and public viewers receive sanitized records
and visibility-controlled summaries. WebSocket updates carry invalidations,
not response content.

Interactive definitions enforce bounded fields/options, supported field types,
status, result visibility, response limits, answer types, URLs, dates, times,
numeric bounds, record capacity, and Q&A moderation states.
